{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_17_audit_fix_round_2_design", "label": "Second Audit-Fix Round Design", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-17-audit-fix-round-2-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concept_submissions_scoping_fix", "label": "/api/submissions Unscoped GET/DELETE Fix", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "GET/DELETE /api/submissions matched everything when called with an empty filter, letting any visitor of any exported site enumerate or wipe all form submissions across every project. Fix requires a non-empty project_id or form_name else 400; the Inbox UI is scoped to the current project instead of a global cross-project view \u2014 a deliberate, discussed behavior change.", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-17-audit-fix-round-2-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concept_escapehtml_shared_utility", "label": "Shared escapeHtml Utility", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Three separate, non-shared HTML-escaping implementations (forms.js's escape, exportHtml.js's escAttr, cart.js's inline runtime esc()) meant most free-text-to-HTML interpolation sites never escaped at all, causing stored XSS. Consolidated into frontend/src/lib/escapeHtml.js exporting escAttr (attribute-safe) and escText (text-safe), applied at every previously-unescaped site.", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-17-audit-fix-round-2-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "frontend_src_lib_escapehtml_escattr", "label": "escAttr()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-17-audit-fix-round-2-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "fronte